From 728c81f64ee8ad83ca5fabafcacaeb7bcd8b94c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viktor Semykin <thesame.ml@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:03:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/gma500: add opt-in Cedarview MSVDX H.264 decoding

Host MSVDX beside its existing PCI/display owner. Admit bounded H.264
picture state, own MMU/storage, export writable decoded images and
initialized format probes, and checkpoint before suspend. Unproved
quiescence quarantines DMA storage.

The private interface is root-only and disabled until msvdx=1. This is a
downstream prototype ABI, not a mainline media API. No firmware binary
or sample picture is included.

Validated on N2800 with software-reference NV12 comparisons,
boundary/rejection inputs, sequence wrap, writable imports, exact GPU
plane sampling and native Wayland presentation. The separate mpv chroma
fix is necessary for correct GL2/GLES2 imported colors.

Signed-off-by: Viktor Semykin <thesame.ml@gmail.com>
