index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..c9069fd90702b73e022c3926775728f52aaee31e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/gpu/gma500-msvdx.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,126 @@
+.. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+
+Cedarview MSVDX H.264 decoding
+=============================
+
+This optional gma500 host supports the MSVDX 2.1.3 decoder on Intel Atom N2800
+(PCI 8086:0be2). Build with ``CONFIG_DRM_GMA500_MSVDX=y`` (default n), then enable it with
+``gma500_gfx.msvdx=1``. It uses a separate
+register window and owned MMU mappings; it does not reset the SGX or display.
+Firmware is loaded on the first picture submission.
+
+Userspace and trust boundary
+---------------------------
+
+The companion cedar-video project supplies a VA-API backend and root broker.
+The private ``/dev/cedar-msvdx`` interface remains mode 0600 and requires
+CAP_SYS_RAWIO. The broker authorizes one desktop UID and serves one decoder
+client. Root is trusted. This is a downstream interface for powervr_sgx, not
+a stable mainline DRM/media ABI or a general multi-user decoder service.
+
+Packets contain bounded H.264 picture descriptions and file-local surface
+handles, not arbitrary commands, registers or physical addresses. The host
+validates geometry, references, slice boundaries and limits before submission.
+Unsupported input fails; the supplied player disables software fallback.
+
+Input and storage
+-----------------
+
+Supported input is progressive 8-bit H.264 4:2:0 through coded 1920x1088,
+including restricted Baseline/Main/High, four short-term references, reference
+B pictures and weighted prediction. Interlacing, long-term references, custom
+scaling matrices and other codecs are unsupported. A picture has at most 64
+slices and approximately 1 MiB of compressed data including packet overhead.
+
+Image backing uses stride 1920 and UV offset 2088960 even for smaller pictures.
+Five bounded image/motion slots retain the decoded reference state. Completed
+DMA-BUFs retain storage independently of the decoder file and prevent output
+slot reuse until their external references retire. CPU download packs the
+logical rectangle. Undecoded VA probes have independent initialized backing;
+they do not start the engine or mark the surface decoded.
+
+``CEDAR_CAP_WRITABLE_EXPORT`` advertises conventional O_RDWR image sharing.
+VA access flags are usage hints, not an enforced immutability guarantee. CPU
+access must use DMA-BUF synchronization; callers must finish external writes
+before decoder use, including reference-picture reads. Only image pages are
+exported. Motion and command storage remain private. Coherent image allocations
+match cached CPU mappings, with cache maintenance at CPU/device access boundaries.
+Motion and command storage use write-combined mappings. CPU-only page-descriptor
+arrays use virtual-contiguity allocation with vmalloc fallback; hardware sees
+the separately allocated DMA pages, not those descriptor arrays.
+
+Completion is polled synchronously with bounded waits. Closing or suspending
+must prove engine quiescence before unmapping DMA pages. An unproved shutdown
+quarantines the engine and retains its memory, device and module references;
+reboot is the recovery. A single startup retry is limited to a fresh intra
+command that was unconsumed before a verified isolated reset. Established
+reference chains are not replayed. Suspend retains images, motion and software
+DPB state; the next submission reloads firmware and scratch state.
+
+Firmware and command provenance
+-------------------------------
+
+The unchanged vendor image is requested as
+``cedarview/msvdx_fw_mfld_DE2.0.bin``, version 0x496, 32788 bytes,
+SHA256 ``6d073592a1f10bc7da269f11fd8f15b6ca3e69c07d9efde4cdaa10f4af6be27b``.
+It is supplied separately under its vendor redistribution license. No firmware
+binary is included in this patch.
+
+The runtime template and VLC tables derive from the published Intel/Imagination
+DE2 psb_video source at commit fa6f2e9012a890942a47eae9f6f1a0ddcd97e9a4:
+
+https://android.googlesource.com/platform/hardware/intel/img/psb_video/+/fa6f2e9012a890942a47eae9f6f1a0ddcd97e9a4/
+
+The licensed notices remain with the tables. The template contains no sample
+bitstream or reference image; picture state and caller input are supplied at
+runtime. Firmware RAM transfer follows the public GPL Cedarview DDK
+imgv/psb_msvdxinit.c; register offsets follow imgv/psb_msvdx.h, from
+https://github.com/thomas001/cdv/tree/a0f0aa899a67cdd23adfd3a2fc0ab7956eb90cc9/imgv.
+
+Checking changes
+----------------
+
+Build against the exact target kernel configuration and Module.symvers.
+The companion tools compare complete visible NV12 frames with software, check
+hardware completion counters, reject unsupported controls and verify storage
+retirement. Cover profiles, crops, 1088 coded lines, reference B pictures,
+64-slice inputs, seek/reload and 16-bit firmware sequence wrap. A live-reference
+suspend check requires an explicit operator request.
+
+Presentation is separate from decoding. CPU-copy playback downloads and uploads
+NV12. Optional zero-copy playback needs Mesa R8/GR88 sampling and corrected
+mpv imported-chroma metadata. No read-only SGX import patches are required.
+Both paths require SGX_DEBUG=serial in compositor and player to avoid tile
+tearing/reordering. Zero dropped-frame counters do not detect
+that corruption. Keep a bootable fallback when replacing gma500.
+
+Template regeneration
+---------------------
+
+The checked-in ``msvdx-template.json`` is the declarative command layout and
+patch-index source. The generator reads VLC data from the pinned public
+``pnw_H264.c``; its SHA256 is checked before generating. No firmware, media,
+decoded reference image or encoder is involved. From the gma500 directory::
+
+  python3 generate-msvdx-template.py --source /path/to/pnw_H264.c \
+    --layout msvdx-template.json --output cdv_h264_template.h --check
+
+Omit ``--check`` to regenerate after an intentional layout change. Review
+command lengths, patch indices, GPU addresses and capacities together. The
+runtime host supplies all picture/slice state and bitstream bytes.
+
+Resource and failure limits
+---------------------------
+
+At most 64 image/motion allocations exist globally, including detached exports
+and independent initialized images used for format probes. Each owns
+1024 pages (4 MiB at 4 KiB pages); this bounds DMA32 image/motion storage to
+256 MiB. Engine command, RENDEC and bitstream allocations are separate bounded
+resources. Probe allocations retire with their last external reference; no
+shared black allocation remains cached after all clients close.
+
+DMA-BUF release uses atomic reader accounting and never takes the mutex held
+while firmware is polled. Quarantine prevents new work until reboot. Sleep may
+retry a bounded reset/drain proof; after a successful proof it can proceed while
+all quarantined allocations remain retained. An unsuccessful proof still refuses
+power-down rather than risking DMA into released memory.
